{"overview":"Karin Daughter of Ingmar is a 1920 Swedish silent drama film directed by Victor Sjöström. It is the second part in Sjöström's large-scale adaption of Selma Lagerlöf's novel Jerusalem, following Sons of Ingmar from the year before, and depicting chapter three and four from the novel. The critical reception was however unenthusiastic and Sjöström decided to not direct any more parts.","cast":[{"n":"Tora Teje","c":"Karin Ingmarsdotter","p":"/tTTwDxGBkWike9y4CKZjrxO8kDj.jpg","q":"Q3437434"},{"n":"Victor Sjöström","c":"Stor Ingmar","p":"/iGtT2mbmLt80YPk9lXJRSyxaEKW.jpg","q":"Q55170"},{"n":"Bertil Malmstedt","c":"Lill-Ingmar","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Nils Lundell","c":"Eljas Elof Ersson","p":"/xmuQ3sf6Se2IbVtGUeFN4o4sTuY.jpg","q":"Q5966388"},{"n":"Tor Weijden","c":"Halfvor","p":"/nD4h3Svzbk8gYkcjcPjHnAr7LIX.jpg","q":"Q6234505"},{"n":"Emil Fjellström","c":"Stark-Ingmar","p":"/f6HU6bSruq4SHOU0GiU85vZhV6p.jpg","q":"Q5732358"},{"n":"Nils Aréhn","c":"Berger Sven Persson","p":"/8iKENizuIar1yrLuVm2hyuIivrx.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Josua Bengtson","c":"Eljas' friend","p":"/tYK08uJWrpxgb0zq4apnMGQpXjy.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Bror Berger","c":"Horse-dealer","p":"/2wv6aHogiuy2Fw0wCfB5wApQLf5.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Harriet Bosse","c":"Brita","p":"/6rDt49lZdqravtMhSLVAGB2i5Z0.jpg","q":null}],"country":["Sweden"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karin,_Daughter_of_Ingmar","qid":"Q1761917","rel":{"SE":{"d":"1920-02-02"}},"stills":["silent-karin-ingmarsdotter_1.webp","silent-karin-ingmarsdotter_2.webp","silent-karin-ingmarsdotter_3.webp","silent-karin-ingmarsdotter_4.webp"]}